## reading (written after the results above)
- Original tests under specialists fail on BOTH refs with the same assertion: 'no code to run' == 'RuntimeError'/'TimeoutError'. The injected crash never fired (only real_agents._dispatch was patched; the specialist template calls real_dispatcher.dispatch), so the real test_runner ran and refused a missing code. The cause is the fixture/patch, not a behavior defect. The failure is also identical before and after the R-157 adapter, so it could not tell a leaking runtime from a correct one.
- Fixed tests (helper patches both bindings, assertions unchanged) pass in both runtimes at 573793c.
- Fixed tests FAIL under specialists at 228b956 (before the R-157 adapter) with the raw exception text and the secret marker in the result. They also kill the mutant that reverts the adapter in the branch, so they detect the real leak R-157 fixed. The fix makes the tests discriminating, not weaker.
- tests/test_r158_gap_regressions.py::test_g157_5_* also kills the mutant (1 failed) and passes on the restored code.
